DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("cos(((sqrt(x))/2))");
$fun_1 = Formula("(((sqrt(x)))^2)^5");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("([3, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (([3, 12] U ({-1, 3, 4, 6, 8}))))) U [3, 12] U [3, 12] U [3, 12]");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-1, 3, 4, 6, 8} U (7, infinity) U (7, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 19] U (-infinity, 19]");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(((0, 10) U (0, 10)) U (-infinity, 19]) U (-infinity, 19]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Lily had [`3`] colored pencils. Her teacher gave her [`8`] more pencils and asked her to share them equally with her best friend. After sharing, how many colored pencils does Lily have in total?

[_____]{7}
[%
3+8/2

First, calculate how many pencils Lily gets from sharing: 8 ÷ 2 = 4 pencils. Then, add the pencils she originally had: 3 + 4 = 7 pencils.
%]
---

During art class, Emma brought [`4`] sheets of origami paper. Her tablemate gave her [`11`] more sheets to help with her project. How many sheets of origami paper does Emma have now?

[_____]{15}
[%
4+11

Add the two amounts together: 4 + 11 = 15 sheets of origami paper.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 19\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 0 < x < 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`((B \cup B) \cup A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 6\}`]
- [`B = \{-1, 3, 4, 6, 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 12\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C \cap ((C \cup (B)))) \cup C \cup C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, 4, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, -3, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, -2, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, 4, 4>") . Compute("<7, -2, -1>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -3, 9>") . Compute("<7, -2, -1>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, 4, 4>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, 4, 4>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 1, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 7, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 1, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, 1, 3>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, 1, 3>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 7, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, 1, 3>") x Compute("<2, 7, 3>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>4)}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
